<title>PHILIPPINES: Victorias VMC unit details debt to 10 creditors.</title>
<headline>Victorias VMC unit details debt to 10 creditors.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>North Negros Marketing Co Inc, a unit of Philippine sugar miller Victorias Milling Corp, said on Monday its total liabilities reached 2.196 billion pesos against total assets of 2.1 billion.</p>
<p>In a statement to the Securities and Exchange Commission,</p>
<p>North Negros gave details of its liabilities as of March 31.</p>
<p>LOANS PAYABLE (in million pesos)</p>
<p>Asian Bank Corp						  131.63</p>
<p>Asia Trust Development Bank				   18.91</p>
<p>Bank of the Philippine Islands			     240.00</p>
<p>Dao Heng Bank						    100.00</p>
<p>Land Bank of the Philippines				 440.76</p>
<p>Metropolitan Bank and Trust Co			     592.65</p>
<p>Philippine National Bank				     223.93</p>
<p>Philippine Commercial International Bank		 100.00</p>
<p>Philippine Commercial Capital Inc			   11.42</p>
<p>United Pacific Capital Corp				    4.81</p>
<p>TOTAL BANK LOANS						  1,864</p>
<p>ACCOUNTS PAYABLE AND ACCRUED EXPENSE		     253.45</p>
<p>CURRENT PORTION OF INSTALLMENT PAYABLE		    57.29</p>
<p>OBLIGATION UNDER CAPITAL LEASE				13.20</p>
<p>CURRENT PORTION OF OBLIGATION UNDER CAPITAL LEASE	8.33</p>
<p>TOTAL LIABILITIES						 2,196</p>
<p>--Manila newsroom (63 2) 841-8936, Fax 817-6267</p>
</text>
